        sol_biogas_faq_kicker: "Frequently asked questions",
        sol_biogas_faq_title: "What they ask most.",
        sol_biogas_faq_q1: "How long does a basic design take?",
        sol_biogas_faq_a1: "8 to 14 weeks from signing. More complex projects may take up to 18 weeks.",
        sol_biogas_faq_q2: "Does 4WaTT design for all types of waste?",
        sol_biogas_faq_a2: "Yes. We have experience with cattle, swine, poultry, slaughterhouses, sugarcane vinasse, MSW, WWTP sludge and industrial waste.",
        sol_biogas_faq_q3: "What is included in the feasibility study?",
        sol_biogas_faq_a3: "Substrate survey and analysis, generation sizing, energy use analysis, CAPEX/OPEX, financial model with IRR/NPV/payback, sensitivity analysis and technology recommendation, formatted for presentation to financiers.",
        sol_biogas_faq_q4: "Do you work with environmental licensing?",
        sol_biogas_faq_a4: "In partnership with specialized firms. The basic design is conceived with environmental requirements in mind, supported by RAP, emissions data and mass flows.",
        sol_biogas_faq_q5: "What is the difference between basic and executive design?",
        sol_biogas_faq_a5: "The basic design defines what will be built and how (technologies, equipment, layout, specifications, cost). The executive design details how to build (calculation reports, detailing, documents for execution without ambiguity). BNDES usually requires the complete executive design.",
        sol_biogas_faq_q6: "Doesn't the free simulator already give me the feasibility?",
        sol_biogas_faq_a6: "The simulator delivers a market estimate in minutes — useful to rule out unviable projects. But the numbers a bank accepts for credit release require substrate survey, financial modeling with IRR/NPV/payback, ART and technical documentation. That is what the 4WaTT Investment Project delivers.",
        sol_biogas_faq_q7: "How is the Investment Project paid?",
        sol_biogas_faq_a7: "The project entry fee can be paid in installments along the delivery milestones (feasibility, basic design and financial modeling). Construction itself is financed by third parties; the client needs cash for the entry fee, not for the full construction.",
