        sol_biometano_publico_industria_desc: "Replacement of fossil natural gas, emissions reduction and access to low-carbon markets.",
        sol_biometano_publico_frotas_name: "Bus and truck fleets",
        sol_biometano_publico_frotas_desc: "Biomethane as vehicular CNG for urban and intercity fleets · lower cost and less CO₂.",
        sol_biometano_publico_geracao_name: "Power generation",
        sol_biometano_publico_geracao_desc: "Fuel for generator sets or gas turbines, with high energy density.",
        sol_biometano_publico_distribuidoras_name: "Gas distributors",
        sol_biometano_publico_distribuidoras_desc: "Injection into the grid to meet biofuel targets and decarbonize the portfolio.",
        sol_biometano_publico_condominios_name: "Condominiums and restaurants",
        sol_biometano_publico_condominios_desc: "LPG replacement for kitchens, cleaning and showers.",
        sol_biometano_faq_kicker: "Frequently asked questions",
        sol_biometano_faq_title: "What they ask most.",
        sol_biometano_faq_q1: "What is the difference between biogas and biomethane?",
        sol_biometano_faq_a1: "Biogas is produced directly by the biodigester (55–70% CH₄, 30–45% CO₂ and impurities). Biomethane is biogas after upgrading (97%+ methane), equivalent to natural gas, and can be injected into the grid or used as vehicular fuel.",
        sol_biometano_faq_q2: "How does ANP 854/2021 regulation work?",
        sol_biometano_faq_a2: "It establishes (1) quality specifications; (2) requirements for producer registration; (3) rules for the fiscal measurement system; (4) procedures for periodic laboratory analysis. 4WaTT accompanies the entire registration and compliance process.",
        sol_biometano_faq_q3: "How to commercialize the biomethane produced?",
        sol_biometano_faq_a3: "Four alternatives: direct sale to an industrial consumer via dedicated pipeline; injection into the concessionaire's grid; compression for CNG (fleets); liquefaction for LNG (trucks). 4WaTT structures the commercial model together with the technical project.",
        sol_biometano_faq_q4: "What is a CBIO and how much is it worth?",
        sol_biometano_faq_a4: "The CBIO (Decarbonization Credit) is a RenovaBio financial asset. 1 CBIO = 1 tonne of CO₂e avoided, traded on B3, with a historical value of R$ 50 to R$ 200. RenovaBio producers issue them automatically, proportional to verified production.",
        sol_biometano_faq_q5: "What is the minimum volume to make a plant viable?",
        sol_biometano_faq_a5: "Economic viability typically starts from 500 Nm³/day of biomethane. Below this, fixed costs of equipment, maintenance and certification compromise returns. Plants between 500 and 5,000 Nm³/day have the best indicators. 4WaTT performs the specific sizing.",
        sol_biometano_cta_kicker: "Next step",
        sol_biometano_cta_title: "I want to produce biomethane.",
